title: Math::Min accepts vec3 arguments despite having no vec3 binding
updated_at: "2026-09-08T19:13:22Z"
---
Reported 2026-09-09. The call  should produce a compiler error because Openplanet's Math::Min bindings are scalar-only. The checker treated resolved named/object arguments against primitive overload parameters as neutral during external overload-set resolution, so no NoMatchingSignatures diagnostic was emitted. Fixed with a regression test covering vec2/vec3/vec4/quat rejection and int/float controls, plus concrete named-to-primitive incompatibility rejection in the overload checker.